# Guitar (issues 107, redrawn): 1x1 tile at the south wall (col 1, row 6 of the main room). Drawn on its own, no stand: the body sits north-east with its dark sound hole and the neck runs south-west to the headstock and mist tuners, lit from the top-left. The stand is not part of this picture on purpose (Marc, 2026-10-28): while the guitar is played the pose sprite `player-guitar` replaces this piece and draws the empty stand under the player, so it reads as the guitar lifted off its stand.
size: 16x16
